==Battleground==
*1 [[Elephantidae Papaou]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*20 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 11.33 seconds<sup>340f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*8 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
*2 [[Suidae Piggicus|Suidae Piggici]] spawn after 76.67 seconds<sup>2,300f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
*3 [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn after 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Although this stage might ''seem'' rushable at first, due to the boss's obscene health pool of 2,000,000, you are '''going''' to fight every peon in this stage over the course of several minutes.
The general idea is to use units like Slime & Awakened Bahamut to take out the more problematic enemies (especially Bore Jr.) while slowly chipping down the boss with Courier.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier is an essential part of whatever your strategy ends up being and will likely serve as your main damage against the boss, as it can hit the boss reasonably consistently and with its Behemoth Slayer ability, those hits go from being totally insignificant to just marginally insignificant, meaning that you can actually kill the thing. Also decent at clearing Mr. Angels and Angelic Hippoes.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Very resistant against the angel enemies and has a high pool of health that means it can hold back every enemy in the stage except for Bore Jr. Can also survive a hit from the boss at level 30, or with max health talents it can survive 2 hits at level 38 and above.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Jelly Dumpling acts as a very consistent way to clear peons right at the start of the stage and transitions into a very inconsistent and situational nuker on the bigger enemies that come later in the stage. At level 50, Jelly Dumpling's wave can nearly 2-shot Bore Jr. with the difference being made up by either Courier or Ramen chip. Beware of a few things, however. One: Ramen is dumb and stupid and evil and likes to make Jelly Dumpling miss very frequently, do not deploy it if the enemy at the direct frontline has a lot of knockbacks. Two: Jelly Dumpling needs either very precise timing and/or luck to get a hit in if a Pigicus is at the frontline, if Loris is at the backline, or if you have pushed into Eliphantidae's range. In these scenarios, spawning Jelly Dumpling is usually just going to be a waste of money.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]: Awakened Bahamut, especially with talents can act as a sort of emergency button when things go awry. It can clear out most enemies in this level almost immediately and give you back a lot of lost ground, as well as one-shotting Bore Jr. Be careful of Bore Jr's mini wave, as if can completely screw your timing if you aren't careful. Bahamut also has a hard time reaching the boss or Pigicus without being juggled, so don't expect too much value on those.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - Thanks to Cosmo's very high standing range of 850, he's able to out-range every enemy here, even Loris. When he lands an attack, his [[Wave Attack]] has enough damage to one-shot Bore Jr. and deal great damage to all other threats. Even though Papaou is [[Wave Immune]], Cosmo can greatly chip him down over time.

